# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Gig Solutions — Environment Variables
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ONLY ONE env var is needed: DATABASE_URL
# All other secrets (Resend API key, sender address) are hardcoded.
#
# ─── HOW TO SET UP ON VERCEL ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. Create a free PostgreSQL database:
#    - Vercel Postgres: https://vercel.com/docs/storage/vercel-postgres
#    - Neon (free 0.5GB): https://neon.tech
#    - Supabase (free 500MB): https://supabase.com
#
# 2. Copy the connection string (looks like):
#    postgresql://user:password@host:port/database?schema=public
#
# 3. In Vercel: Project Settings → Environment Variables
#    Key:   DATABASE_URL
#    Value: postgresql://user:password@host:port/database?schema=public
#
# 4. Push the database schema:
#    npx prisma db push
#    (run this locally with DATABASE_URL set in .env)
#
# ─── FOR LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the DATABASE_URL:
#    cp .env.example .env
#    # Then edit .env with your database URL
#
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:port/database?schema=public"
